# React and TypeScript Style Rules

Read and follow the root `AGENTS.md` file before modifying any code in this
repository. It is the canonical source of engineering standards.

## Key Rules

- Preserve application behaviour. Do not refactor architecture beyond the task.
- Use the configured Prettier formatter (`npm run format`).
- Use the configured ESLint linter (`npm run lint`).
- Follow the import ordering conventions in AGENTS.md.
- Use descriptive names. Booleans should start with `is`, `has`, `can`,
  `should`, or `was`.
- Prefer guard clauses over deep nesting.
- Never use nested ternaries.
- Type component props with explicit interfaces.
- Avoid `any`. Prefer `unknown` followed by validation.
- Use `import type` for type-only imports.
- One persistent `<Canvas>`, renderer-agnostic navigation, demand-driven
  render scheduling.
- Use **npm** as the package manager.
